---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";
---

<Legal
  title="Terms"
  description="Dunlin is free, open source software under the MIT License. The public beta is provided as is, without warranty."
  eyebrow="Legal · Terms"
>
  <h2>Open source</h2>
  <p>
    Dunlin is free software released under the
    <a href={site.license} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      MIT License
    </a>
    . You may use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense and sell
    copies of the software under the terms of that license.
  </p>

  <h2>Beta software</h2>
  <p>
    The public beta is provided “as is”, without warranty of any kind, express
    or implied. It is an early build. Back up your work and do not use it for
    anything you cannot afford to lose.
  </p>

  <h2>No service</h2>
  <p>
    Dunlin does not operate a hosted service for your projects or sessions. The
    optional relay is software you run yourself. You are responsible for the
    machine, network, accounts, access control, backups and credentials of that
    relay.
  </p>

  <h2>macOS and Gatekeeper</h2>
  <p>
    Beta builds are ad-hoc signed until an Apple Developer ID is available.
    macOS may require you to approve the app in System Settings, Privacy &amp;
    Security. Only download Dunlin from the official GitHub releases page.
  </p>

  <h2>Third party harnesses</h2>
  <p>
    OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex and other harnesses are separate products with
    their own terms, licenses and privacy policies. Dunlin is not affiliated
    with OpenCode, Anthropic, or OpenAI.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may change as the project grows. The current version is always
    published on this page. Questions: open an issue at
    <a href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      {site.github.replace("https://", "")}
    </a>
    .
  </p>
</Legal>
